<title>INDIA: RBI sets 91-day t-bill cut-off at 98.34 rupees.</title>
<headline>RBI sets 91-day t-bill cut-off at 98.34 rupees.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) officially revised figures of bids accepted at Friday's 91-day t-bill auction.</p>
<p>In a late night statement on Friday, the central bank said it accepted competitive bids for 72 million rupees and non competitive bids for 1,428 million rupees, correcting earlier figures of 69.10 million rupees and 1,430.90 million respectively.</p>
<p>The RBI said it set the cut-off at 98.34 rupees in the 91-day t-bill auction against 98.47 rupees a week ago.</p>
<p>The yield rose to 6.77 percent from 6.23 percent a week ago, dealers said.</p>
